From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:04:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: rtkit: Let a shut-down co-processor's mailbox
 stop

apple_rtkit_shutdown() ends in apple_rtkit_reinit(), which starts the
mailbox again, so the mailbox holds a runtime-PM reference for as long
as the RTKit instance exists. A shut-down co-processor sends nothing,
but its mailbox then keeps the power domain it shares with it on: the
A10 GPU's runtime suspend leaves ps_gfx powered through its mailbox.

Add apple_rtkit_mbox_stop() for a co-processor that is not running. It
stops the mailbox until apple_rtkit_reinit() starts it again. Mailbox
start and stop already ignore a repeated call, so reinit and free need
no change, and callers that don't use it see none.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c       | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
index a6bce181d988..725ab3fa7762 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
@@ -776,6 +776,26 @@ int apple_rtkit_reinit(struct apple_rtkit *rtk)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_rtkit_reinit);
 
+/**
+ * apple_rtkit_mbox_stop() - Stop the mailbox of a co-processor that is shut down
+ * @rtk: RTKit reference, after apple_rtkit_shutdown()
+ *
+ * A shut-down co-processor sends nothing, but its mailbox stays started and
+ * so keeps its power domain on. Stop it until apple_rtkit_reinit(), which
+ * the caller runs before starting the co-processor again.
+ *
+ * Return: 0, or -EBUSY while the co-processor runs.
+ */
+int apple_rtkit_mbox_stop(struct apple_rtkit *rtk)
+{
+	if (apple_rtkit_is_running(rtk))
+		return -EBUSY;
+	apple_mbox_stop(rtk->mbox);
+	flush_workqueue(rtk->wq);
+	return 0;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_rtkit_mbox_stop);
+
 static int apple_rtkit_set_ap_power_state(struct apple_rtkit *rtk,
 					  unsigned int state)
 {
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h
index dde8abe99d00..1f9ebb6187fb 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h
@@ -125,6 +125,12 @@ int apple_rtkit_wake(struct apple_rtkit *rtk);
  */
 int apple_rtkit_shutdown(struct apple_rtkit *rtk);
 
+/*
+ * Stop the mailbox of a shut-down co-processor, so that its power domain can
+ * go off; apple_rtkit_reinit() starts it again.
+ */
+int apple_rtkit_mbox_stop(struct apple_rtkit *rtk);
+
 /*
  * Put the co-processor into the lowest power state. Note that it usually
  * is not possible to recover from this state without a full SoC reset.
